course: dictionary
lesson: 4095
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Gin» is one of them. You cannot know which meaning is right until you read the words around it, which are its context.
explain: «The cotton gin separated the fibres from the seeds.» Cotton, fibres and seeds are the clues. A cotton gin is a machine, not a drink. Always ask: which meaning would make sense in this sentence?
explain: «Gin is a drink for adults only, so children must never touch it.» The clue is adults only. This gin is a strong alcoholic drink. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: «Dad shuffled the cards for a game of gin after tea.» The clue is the game and the cards. Here gin is a card game. The same word can mean a drink, a machine, a trap or a game, so always read on.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant.
fact: «Gin» means a strong, clear alcoholic drink flavoured with juniper berries; it is for adults only.
fact: A «cotton gin» is a machine that separates cotton fibres from the seeds. Eli Whitney made one in 1793.
fact: «Gin» can also mean an old trap for catching animals, or a card game called gin rummy.
fact: Gin has one syllable and ends in a vowel and a consonant, so its verb doubles the n: «ginned», «ginning» (rare).
exercise: «The cotton gin made cotton farming faster.» What is a cotton gin? | A strong drink flavoured with juniper berries | A card game played with a pack | A trap for catching animals | *A machine that separates cotton fibres from the seeds
exercise: «Gin is a drink for adults only, so children must never touch it.» What kind of thing is gin here? | A machine for cotton | A trap for animals | A card game | *A strong alcoholic drink
exercise: Dad asks, «Shall we have a game of gin after tea?» What does gin mean here? | A strong drink for adults | *A card game | A trap for animals | A machine for seeds
test: «The farmer set a gin in the wood to catch foxes.» What does gin mean in this sentence? | A strong, clear drink | *A trap for catching animals | A machine for cotton | A card game
test: «The bottle of gin was for grown-ups only.» What clue tells you that gin is a drink? | Set in the wood | Cotton and seeds | Played after tea | *Bottle and grown-ups only
exam: Which meaning of gin fits «Gin is a drink for adults only, not for children»? | A machine that separates cotton from seeds | A trap for catching animals | *A strong alcoholic drink | A card game
